<file path="coding-agent-testing-error-code/README.md">
# Buggy Test Suite (New Benchmark Examples)

This is a **standalone** folder of small Python repos, each with one
seeded bug and a pytest test suite that fails because of it. It is
meant to be uploaded as its own GitHub repo (or dropped into
`my-buggy-test-repo/examples/` if you'd rather point the agent at
this folder directly) so you can run your autonomous coding agent
against fresh, unseen examples.

No files from your original project were modified — this is entirely
separate.

## Layout

```
examples/
  11_temperature_converter/   wrong formula (numeric logic bug)
  12_stack_queue/              Queue.dequeue() pops wrong end (FIFO -> LIFO)
  13_url_shortener/            every URL overwrites the same dict key
  14_grade_calculator/         classic mutable default argument bug
  15_config_parser/            bare except silently swallows bad input
  16_prime_checker/            off-by-one in sqrt(n) loop boundary
```

Each example folder is self-contained:
- one (or two) source file(s) with a single seeded bug
- a `test_*.py` file exercising that bug
- a `pytest.ini`

Every example was verified locally: each fails 1+ tests due to the
bug, with the rest passing, confirming the tests target the bug and
nothing else.

## How to use with your agent

Point `--repo` (or `--benchmark-dir`) at one of these example
folders, e.g.:

```bash
python main.py --repo /path/to/buggy-test-suite/examples/11_temperature_converter --goal "fix all failing unit tests"
```

Or run the whole set through the benchmark harness if you copy this
`examples/` folder alongside (or in place of) the existing
`my-buggy-test-repo/examples/` directory:

```bash
python main.py --benchmark --benchmark-dir ./buggy-test-suite/examples
```

## Bug summary

| Folder | Bug type | What's wrong |
|---|---|---|
| 11_temperature_converter | Logic error | `celsius_to_fahrenheit` uses the wrong formula |
| 12_stack_queue | Logic error | `Queue.dequeue()` pops from the end instead of the front |
| 13_url_shortener | Logic error | `shorten()` writes to a hardcoded dict key, overwriting prior entries |
| 14_grade_calculator | Classic Python pitfall | Mutable default argument (`history=[]`) shared across calls |
| 15_config_parser | Silent failure | Bare `except` swallows malformed lines instead of raising |
| 16_prime_checker | Off-by-one | Loop range excludes `sqrt(n)`, so perfect squares of primes (25, 49...) are misreported as prime |
</file>

